    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0856" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v07/pg822"/>

                <head>403. Telegram From the Ambassador in Chile (Lyon) to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d403-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-02-21T11:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                                1957—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>436. Reference proposal invite President Ibanez visit US. Embassy considers
                    important and timely Ibanez now be invited. He has been surprisingly and
                    gratifyingly unwavering in anti-inflationary fight, and invitation would
                    constitute our endorsement and support Chile’s action this program which can
                    serve as example Latin America and rest world. Invitation should also assure
                    continuance program after elections and would give lift to Chile’s morale which
                    needed this juncture due to decline copper price, difficult nitrate situation
                    and general political picture. It would also constitute valuable psychological
                    counter frequent charges here and other American Republics that US more
                    sympathetic hemisphere dictatorships than to democracies.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d403-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Lyon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d403-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d403-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 725.11/2–2157. Confidential.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d403-f2" n="2" xml:id="d403-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 428 to Santiago, March 7, the Department informed Lyon that an
                    invitation to Ibáñez was under consideration, but that a decision was not
                    expected before the middle of March. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
